[statement]
A removal goes, at the latest, just before the walk placing a package
that provides a name it provides, at no version too: `ax`, which `y`
needed through `v`, a name `ax` provides at a version, would be removed
last
(`a-package-needed-through-a-name-it-provides-at-a-version-is-removed-last`),
but `n`, requested, provides `nov`, as `ax` does, and apk removes `ax`
just before installing `n`, after `b`.

